"comparison": "Both BAC and MS describe the treatment of loan origination costs for Loans Held-for-Sale (LHFS) carried at the lower of cost or fair value. BAC states that origination costs are capitalized into the loan's carrying value and recognized as part of gain or loss upon sale. Similarly, MS states that origination fees or costs are deferred as an adjustment to the loan's cost basis until sale, where they are included in the determination of lower of cost or fair value adjustments and the gain or loss recognized at the time of sale. Both disclosures reflect the same accounting mechanic of deferring costs to adjust the basis/gain/loss upon disposal.",
