"relationship": "same_topic",
"comparison": "Both BAC and JPM disclose the accounting for loan origination costs specifically for LHFS. BAC capitalizes these costs into the carrying value, recognizing them as part of the gain or loss in noninterest income upon sale. JPM similarly defers loan origination fees or costs in a contra loan account until sale, noting that these deferrals are included in the periodic determination of lower of cost or fair value adjustments and/or the gain or loss recognized at the time of sale. The core treatment of capitalizing/deferring costs to adjust the gain/loss upon sale is consistent between the two.",
